    },
    {
      "text": "through separate learnable linear layers, producing a localization token 𝑦𝑝= 𝐸𝑝(𝑝𝑡) and action tokens 𝑦𝑎. To",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "𝜎=(1−𝜎) 𝑦𝑝+ 𝜎𝜖𝑝,",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "𝜎=(1−𝜎) 𝑦𝑜+ 𝜎𝜖𝑜,",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "𝜎=(1−𝜎) 𝑦𝑎+ 𝜎𝜖𝑎.",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "Q = [Qve | Qae],",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "K = [Kve | Kae],",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "V = [Vve | Vae],",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "𝑐= [UMT5(ℓ) | 𝑀𝑠𝑠𝑟",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "Lloc =",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "Lobs = ∥ˆ𝑣𝑜−(𝜖𝑜−𝑦𝑜)∥2 ,",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "Lact = ∥ˆ𝑣𝑎−(𝜖𝑎−𝑦𝑎)∥2 .",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "L = 𝜆𝑝Lloc + 𝜆𝑜Lobs + 𝜆𝑎Lact.",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "at frame index 𝑤0 = 0 and repeatedly performs the same causal inference loop, localizing the robot’s current",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "ˆ𝑦𝑖= Denoise(𝑧𝑑, 𝑧𝑜, 𝑐, ˆ𝑦<𝑖),",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "𝑖∈{𝑝, 𝑜, 𝑎},",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "where ˆ𝑦<𝑖denotes the preceding generated outputs in the causal order 𝑝→𝑜→𝑎. Each denoising process",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "ˆ𝑞𝑡= 𝑤𝑡+ ⌊ˆ𝑝𝑡𝐿⌋,",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "𝑤𝑡+1 = ˆ𝑞𝑡−⌊𝐿/2⌋.",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "∈ℝ𝑑emb of the instruction, and a scene embedding 𝑒img",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "∈ℝ𝑑emb of the initial observation. Qwen3-VL-",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "𝑠𝑖= 𝜔cos(𝑒text",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "https://openreview.net/forum?id=Nu6N69i8SB.",
      "section_id": "sec:references",
      "page_start": 22,
      "page_end": 28
    },
    {
      "text": "position in the last hidden layer, yielding a 𝐷=1,536-dimensional hidden state. A single learnable linear layer",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "projects the hidden state to a 𝑑=128-dimensional embedding, followed by ℓ2 normalization, as formulated in",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "operator formulated in Eq. 3, with softmin temperature 𝛾=1.0. A column-normalization temperature 𝛾𝑓=0.1",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "distance entries scaled by a softmax temperature 𝜅=0.1.",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "𝑖is clamped with 𝜖=10−4 for numerical stability",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "under bfloat16, and the variance regularization weight is 𝜆var=0.001 with label smoothing of 0.1. The path-cost",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "loss weight is 𝜆DTW=0.3, normalized by the sum of sequence lengths 𝑇+𝑁, as formulated in Eq. 10. Both losses",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "Training configuration. The module is trained with AdamW, using 𝛽1=0.9, 𝛽2=0.999, 𝜖=10−8, and weight",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "AdamW (𝛽1=0.9, 𝛽2=0.999, 𝜖=10−8)",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "concatenated in pixel space prior to VAE encoding, producing a combined frame of height 224×3=672 pixels",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "freq_dim =256 to hidden_dim. It is then projected to the six modulation parameters through a SiLU-activated",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "yields one token per timestep, for a total of 𝐻=32 action tokens. The action expert applies one-dimensional",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "weights are linearly interpolated from 𝑑𝑣=3,072 to 𝑑𝑎=1,024 along that dimension. They are then scaled by",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "shift =3.0.",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "Separated (first frame 𝜎=0)",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "Linear interpolation from video expert (𝛼=",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "Weights =0, bias =5.0",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "share an identical training configuration with full-parameter updates. The optimizer is AdamW with 𝛽1=0.9,",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "𝛽2=0.95, and weight decay 10−2. Training uses a constant learning rate of 10−5. Training is distributed across",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "The loss weights are 𝜆𝑜=1.0, 𝜆𝑎=10.0, and 𝜆𝑝=1.0, as formulated in Eq. 16. The elevated action loss weight",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "𝑢∼Uniform[0, 1] and applying the shifted schedule 𝜎= 𝜙(𝑢, 𝑠) = 𝑠· 𝑢/ (1 + (𝑠−1) · 𝑢), where 𝑠is the shift",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "parameter. A Gaussian-weighted importance function 𝑤(𝜎) = exp\u0000−2\u0000(𝜎−𝜎max/2) / 𝜎max",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "AdamW (𝛽1=0.9, 𝛽2=0.95)",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "concatenated in pixel space before VAE encoding, producing a combined frame of height 224 × 3 = 672 pixels.",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "The robot history length is 𝐾=0, meaning only the current frame is used and no historical frames are included.",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "Temporal structure. Each video demonstration window W contains 𝐿=6×32=192 raw video demonstration",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "video ratio of 8:1 produces the 192/8=24 video frames provided to the model. The mapping derived from",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "demonstration frames and robot frames. The resulting target is defined at action resolution and contains 𝐻=32",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "observations are uniformly downsampled at an 8:1 ratio before video encoding, yielding 𝐻/8=4 target frames",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "shift =3.0 for localization and shift =5.0 for visual prediction and action. The inference schedule samples",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "uniform steps from 𝜎=1 to 𝜎=0 and transforms them through the same shifted schedule 𝜙used during training.",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "The predicted action chunk of 𝐻=32 steps is fully executed before the next step. The video demonstration",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "𝑡∈O𝑑, 𝑜𝑟",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "𝑡∈O𝑟",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "𝑡∈S",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    },
    {
      "text": "𝑎𝑡∈A",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix-b",
      "page_start": 32,
      "page_end": 38
    }
